#: ../../technical/articles/012-pdf-summaries-ecb-rates-and-google-sheets-exports.md:28
msgid ""
"There is a spreadsheet formula-injection boundary to resolve. The adapter"
" combines literal value cells with formula cells and sends the whole "
"batch using `USER_ENTERED`, while the value coercer passes strings "
"through unchanged and the formula builder is already separate. If any "
"literal cell can contain untrusted text beginning with `=`, Sheets can "
"interpret it as a formula. The application plan’s input provenance and "
"constraints need to be traced, and literal values should be verified to "
"stay literal (calc_sheets_apply.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/calc_sheets_apply.py`), "
"_calc_sheets_apply_values.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/_calc_sheets_apply_values.py`), "
"_calc_sheets_apply_values.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/_calc_sheets_apply_values.py`))."
msgstr ""
"Tisztázandó egy táblázatképlet-befecskendezési határ. Az adapter a "
"literális értékcellákat képletcellákkal egyesíti, és az egész köteget "
"`USER_ENTERED` módban küldi, miközben az értékkonvertáló változatlanul "
"továbbítja a karakterláncokat, a képletépítő pedig már különálló. Ha "
"bármely literális cella `=` jellel kezdődő nem megbízható szöveget "
"tartalmazhat, a Sheets képletként értelmezheti. Végig kell követni az "
"alkalmazási terv bemeneti származását és korlátait, és ellenőrizni kell, "
"hogy a literális értékek literálisak maradnak-e (calc_sheets_apply.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/calc_sheets_apply.py`), "
"_calc_sheets_apply_values.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/_calc_sheets_apply_values.py`), "
"_calc_sheets_apply_values.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/_calc_sheets_apply_values.py`))."

#: ../../technical/articles/012-pdf-summaries-ecb-rates-and-google-sheets-exports.md:30
msgid ""
"Google request execution names retry semantics explicitly: replay-safe "
"requests receive up to three client retries; single-attempt failures "
"carry an uncertain-effect marker. Most values/clear operations are "
"address-idempotent, but the structural batch is marked `REPLAY_SAFE` "
"while containing `createDeveloperMetadata` requests. Google metadata keys"
" are not unique and the adapter itself deletes prior managed keys to "
"avoid duplicates. If a successful structural write loses its response and"
" is retried internally against the already-fetched spreadsheet snapshot, "
"the same metadata can be created again. This is a concrete conditional "
"mismatch between retry declaration and request semantics. The structural "
"request can also delete protected ranges by description alone; an "
"operator-created range with a matching description could be treated as "
"app-managed. Review both behaviors before relying on the export as an "
"ownership-preserving update (api.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/api.py`), api.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/google/api.py`), calc_sheets_apply.py "
